    ('142c0275-1a5c-47dd-a562-c6874cafa728'::uuid, 'card_description', 'On a high point by the Ridgeway, the hillfort of Liddington Castle hides a pit at least 2.4 metres deep. Its diggers did not reach the bottom, and they interpreted it as a ritual shaft.', 'The earthworks consist of a relatively simple oval bank of timber and earth fronted by a ditch, with opposing causewayed entrances on the east and west sides.', 'teaser-card-s002-rollback:142c0275-1a5c-47dd-a562-c6874cafa728:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s002: card_description ''The earthworks consist of a relatively simple oval bank of timber and earth fronted by a ditch, with opposing causewayed entrances on the east and west sides.'' restored on Liddington Castle', 'b5d139f274be63fb80939445f9bb01d18623e08c0e9b5a1f56daec769746e8ef|c5012b9208a32d628da073fda0a90c02d3770cce662aba0781d81f37ba693282|c5012b9208a32d628da073fda0a90c02d3770cce662aba0781d81f37ba693282', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-write-003", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "On a high point by the Ridgeway, the hillfort of Liddington Castle hides a pit at least 2.4 metres deep. Its diggers did not reach the bottom, and they interpreted it as a ritual shaft."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-check-003 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Liddington Castle is on a high point [S2]; it is by the Ridgeway [S2]; Liddington Castle is a hillfort [S1]; it has a pit at least 2.4 metres deep [S7]; the diggers did not reach the bottom of the pit [S8]; the diggers interpreted the pit as a ritual shaft [S8]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-verify-008 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Liddington Castle is a hillfort in England [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liddington_Castle]; It stands on a high point [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liddington_Castle]; It lies by the Ridgeway [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liddington_Castle]; The hillfort contains a pit at least 2.4 metres deep [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liddington_Castle]; The excavators did not reach the bottom of the pit [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liddington_Castle]; The excavators interpreted the pit as a ritual shaft [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liddington_Castle]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('14aacb74-9cd3-4766-b74b-4911d804c415'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Cattle from North Wales were driven along the Welsh Road to markets in South East England. Its age is not known, yet many lengths follow parish boundaries, hinting at a pre-Roman trackway.', 'Ancient drover''s road moving cattle from Wales to southeastern markets. Merging with Watling Street at Shrewsbury, it passed through Cannock Chase - a well-worn economic artery used for centuries.', 'teaser-card-s002-rollback:14aacb74-9cd3-4766-b74b-4911d804c415:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s002: card_description "Ancient drover''s road moving cattle from Wales to southeastern markets. Merging with Watling Street at Shrewsbury, it passed through Cannock Chase - a well-worn economic artery used for centuries." restored on Welsh Road', '1fb394bfa7ff9b0b46bf72fd3cfd86dfb25eafe6ea0e73a23e0acba78aedb9e7|299f989d91c7996af3fbe9be39e7e428849153c642f05d286cc01e32d0940f49|299f989d91c7996af3fbe9be39e7e428849153c642f05d286cc01e32d0940f49', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-write-003", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Cattle from North Wales were driven along the Welsh Road to markets in South East England. Its age is not known, yet many lengths follow parish boundaries, hinting at a pre-Roman trackway."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-check-003 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "cattle were driven along the Welsh Road [S1, S2]; the cattle came from North Wales [S1]; they were driven to markets in South East England [S1]; the age of the road is not known [S3]; many lengths of the road follow parish boundaries [S4]; this hints at a pre-Roman trackway [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-verify-008 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Welsh Road is a drovers'' road in England [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_Road]; Cattle from North Wales were driven along it [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_Road]; The cattle were taken to markets in South East England [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_Road]; The age of the road is not known [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_Road]; Many lengths of the road follow parish boundaries [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_Road]; This hints that it was a pre-Roman trackway [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_Road]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('1567cad6-7871-428a-b923-946a24ef9b8d'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Where did Krimisa stand? Scholars lean towards Punta Alice, near Cirò Marina, for this town of an indigenous people assimilated by the Greeks, probably born in the 7th century BC.', '7th-century BC city in Calabria, Magna Graecia. Krimisa was inhabited by indigenous people assimilated by the Greeks; thoroughly Hellenized by the Classical period, it remained so into the Roman era.', 'teaser-card-s002-rollback:1567cad6-7871-428a-b923-946a24ef9b8d:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s002: card_description ''7th-century BC city in Calabria, Magna Graecia. Krimisa was inhabited by indigenous people assimilated by the Greeks; thoroughly Hellenized by the Classical period, it remained so into the Roman era.'' restored on Krimisa', '23d943e04d3ca1b4aa1d35cb35d82a4cd6daf7838e0e46be0a74c18e75efb06a|61af4fab07cefef584d4a6383cd4af8f10ac9b7c3ef0c74740ba0bd9ce5e621a|61af4fab07cefef584d4a6383cd4af8f10ac9b7c3ef0c74740ba0bd9ce5e621a', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-write-003", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Where did Krimisa stand? Scholars lean towards Punta Alice, near Cirò Marina, for this town of an indigenous people assimilated by the Greeks, probably born in the 7th century BC."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-check-003 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "where Krimisa stood is uncertain (implied by the question) [S4]; scholars lean towards Punta Alice as its location [S4]; Punta Alice is near Cirò Marina [S4]; Krimisa was a town [S1]; it was a town of an indigenous people assimilated by the Greeks [S2]; it probably originated in the 7th century BC [S1]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-verify-008 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output