    ('16e413ef-7b76-4fda-8f07-5cecf817071d'::uuid, 'card_description', 'In 1949 a woman''s grave of the Roman Iron Age was found at Gårdlösa, a silver fibula with a runic inscription inside. Later digs explored house foundations, grave fields and a shrine.', 'Occupied 1st century BC–11th century AD, this Skåne site yielded a Roman Iron Age grave with a runic-inscribed silver fibula. Excavations revealed house foundations, a grave field, and a shrine.', 'teaser-card-s002-rollback:16e413ef-7b76-4fda-8f07-5cecf817071d:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s002: card_description ''Occupied 1st century BC–11th century AD, this Skåne site yielded a Roman Iron Age grave with a runic-inscribed silver fibula. Excavations revealed house foundations, a grave field, and a shrine.'' restored on Gårdlösa', 'f7e16173ce009836974c41830751f033945d938f5b876595e41c104e9f38a404|ce64adb9843134a2797f8b78546207fe1620c82fd518e94bb775d9409fef65f9|ce64adb9843134a2797f8b78546207fe1620c82fd518e94bb775d9409fef65f9', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-write-003", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "In 1949 a woman''s grave of the Roman Iron Age was found at Gårdlösa, a silver fibula with a runic inscription inside. Later digs explored house foundations, grave fields and a shrine."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-check-003 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "a woman''s grave was found at Gårdlösa in 1949 [S3]; the grave is of the Roman Iron Age [S3]; the grave held a silver fibula [S4]; the fibula bears a runic inscription [S4]; later excavations explored house foundations, grave fields and a shrine [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-verify-009 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Gårdlösa is an Iron Age settlement site in Sweden [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%A5rdl%C3%B6sa]; A grave was found at Gårdlösa in 1949 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%A5rdl%C3%B6sa]; The grave was a woman''s grave [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%A5rdl%C3%B6sa]; The grave dates to the Roman Iron Age [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%A5rdl%C3%B6sa]; The grave contained a silver fibula [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%A5rdl%C3%B6sa]; The fibula bears a runic inscription [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%A5rdl%C3%B6sa]; Later excavations explored house foundations at Gårdlösa [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%A5rdl%C3%B6sa]; Later excavations explored grave fields at Gårdlösa [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%A5rdl%C3%B6sa]; Later excavations explored a shrine at Gårdlösa [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%A5rdl%C3%B6sa]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('17a5dcfe-4f54-467a-9399-ce1a6c72f267'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Outside the walls of Roman Melite, St. Paul''s Catacombs spread through underground galleries and tombs, where tables hewn from the living rock held meals commemorating dead relatives.', 'An underground catacomb complex from the 3rd–8th centuries AD with over 30 hypogea. Some feature agape tables where mourners shared ritual meals with the dead.', 'teaser-card-s002-rollback:17a5dcfe-4f54-467a-9399-ce1a6c72f267:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s002: card_description ''An underground catacomb complex from the 3rd–8th centuries AD with over 30 hypogea. Some feature agape tables where mourners shared ritual meals with the dead.'' restored on St. Paul''s Catacombs', 'd5b4f340f7a96d7ca372109c2b965f9ab981377070593090b9c838aed0857d4c|85f91803af8c5568573c5fcff67edefdbac71a8484f030702d03b67af5d19dc9|85f91803af8c5568573c5fcff67edefdbac71a8484f030702d03b67af5d19dc9', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-write-003", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Outside the walls of Roman Melite, St. Paul''s Catacombs spread through underground galleries and tombs, where tables hewn from the living rock held meals commemorating dead relatives."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-check-003 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "St. Paul''s Catacombs lie outside the walls of Roman Melite [S4]; they consist of underground galleries and tombs [S2]; they contain tables hewn from the living rock [S7]; the tables were used for meals commemorating dead relatives [S7]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-verify-009 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "St. Paul''s Catacombs are catacombs (an underground burial complex) in Malta [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Paul%27s_Catacombs]; St. Paul''s Catacombs lie outside the walls of the Roman city of Melite [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Paul%27s_Catacombs]; The catacombs spread through underground galleries and tombs [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Paul%27s_Catacombs]; The catacombs contain tables hewn from the living rock [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Paul%27s_Catacombs]; These rock-hewn tables were used for meals commemorating dead relatives [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Paul%27s_Catacombs]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('186ef9b5-7a74-43d6-b8d3-f49357ea1304'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Begun under Trajan, the Amphitheatre of Durrës could once hold 20,000 people, the largest Roman amphitheatre ever built in the Balkan Peninsula. A Christian chapel later rose on it.', 'The amphitheatre was built in the beginning of the 2nd century AD, and was used for performances until the 4th century AD.', 'teaser-card-s002-rollback:186ef9b5-7a74-43d6-b8d3-f49357ea1304:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s002: card_description ''The amphitheatre was built in the beginning of the 2nd century AD, and was used for performances until the 4th century AD.'' restored on Amphitheatre of Durrës', 'dfbcdde17e2dd2b0a79a11b02274a965c270c2bd880eee6385a5a3b89fc37b2c|0ec09f33225623a6ea192d3105e49882a101af042ea6e5f27b0e7d3a87ddec94|0ec09f33225623a6ea192d3105e49882a101af042ea6e5f27b0e7d3a87ddec94', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-write-003", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Begun under Trajan, the Amphitheatre of Durrës could once hold 20,000 people, the largest Roman amphitheatre ever built in the Balkan Peninsula. A Christian chapel later rose on it."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-check-003 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "construction of the Amphitheatre of Durrës began under Trajan [S2]; it could once hold 20,000 people [S3]; it is the largest Roman amphitheatre ever built in the Balkan Peninsula [S3]; it is a Roman amphitheatre [S1]; a Christian chapel was later built on it [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-03: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-03-verify-009 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-03/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Amphitheatre of Durrës is a Roman amphitheatre in Durrës, Albania [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.